`latest[name] = { t, id, pos, concl }` — concl is UPPERCASE conclusion or null (when the run has no conclusion yet, i.e., non-terminal: status queued/in_progress → conclusion null → concl null). So:

gateHeld = names.some(c => !latest[c] || latest[c].concl === null)

- missing context (never materialized) → true (ghost gate passes)
- in-progress/queued check run (conclusion null) → true
- terminal success/failure/canceled → false

For gh-682 fixtures: contexts success/failure → concl SUCCESS/FAILURE → gateHeld false → no ghost → no comment. Test 1 passes.
Test 2 "stale CANCELED + fresh green re-stamp": latest sm-liveness concl = SUCCESS (green re-stamp) → gateHeld false → no ghost. Passes.

For gh-757 ghost: required validation check missing from rollup → gateHeld true → ghost probe → re-dispatch. 

Edge — what if the check run exists with concl CANCELED? Then rcCancelled non-empty → old path handles. Fine.

Where to compute: inside the ghost branch, only when rcCancelled.length === 0 (ghost path), and only when rule.requiredContexts exist (rcAny mode: use all contexts on the head; if rollup empty → nothing to wait for → gateHeld false? For anyCancelled ghost: names = Object.keys(latest); if a context is non-terminal → gate held).

Implement helper inline in the ghost branch:

```
// gh-100 ghost gate: re-dispatch is only justified while the merge
// gate is actually WAITING on a required context that will never
// report (missing or non-terminal latest). All-terminal contexts
// (green/failure) mean the gate is not blocked-by-absence — a red
// verdict belongs to fail_validation, a cancelled CONTEXT to the
// rerun path above (gh-682 fixtures).
var gateHeld = false;
try {
   var gateRollup = headCheckRunsSafe(effectiveRepoInfo, rcHead);
   if (gateRollup !== null) {
       var gateLatest = latestCheckRunConclusions(gateRollup);
       var gateNames = rcAny ? Object.keys(gateLatest) : rcContexts;
       gateHeld = gateNames.some(function (c) {
           return !gateLatest[c] || gateLatest[c].concl === null;
       });
   }
} catch (eGate) { gateHeld = false; }
if (!gateHeld) { log 'nothing to rerun' ...; continue; }
```

Wait — careful: if gateRollup probe fails (null), gateHeld stays false → no ghost → logs "nothing to rerun". Acceptable fail-closed? If the check-run probe fails we can't confirm the gate is blocked — safer not to dispatch. But then a real ghost with a flaky probe never heals... The rerun action's own probe failed-open elsewhere. For minimum invasiveness: fail-closed here (no dispatch without evidence the gate is held). Hmm, but in the REAL gh-757 scenario, would the rollup be readable? Yes — `gh pr checks` was readable (it printed "no context reads CANCELED"). OK.

Also note: with gateHeld false we log the same "nothing to rerun" message. Structure:

```
if (ghostProbe && ghostProbe.isGhostCancel && gateHeld) { ...re-dispatch... }
console.log(' ⏭️ ... nothing to rerun');
continue;
```

Need `rcContexts` and `rcAny` in scope — yes (defined above). Also `headCheckRunsSafe` and `latestCheckRunConclusions` are module-level functions in smAgent — in scope.

One more scenario check — the ghost scenario where the required check is PENDING (ghost in_progress check runs, gh-842 family): concl null → gateHeld true → ghost fires → re-dispatch. Correct.

